# Divisibility and number theory, modeled by the kernel. One number DIVIDES another when the second is a multiple of the
# first: d divides n means n = d times k for some k (the witness). The kernel proves the foundational law that divisors are
# closed under addition (if d divides both a and b then d divides their sum), which is just the distributive law, and it
# checks concrete divisibilities by exhibiting the quotient. Divisibility is the spine of number theory: primes, greatest
# common divisors, and modular arithmetic are all built from it.

form natural
  case zero
  case succ
    link prior, like natural

task plus
  take a, like natural
  take b, like natural
  like natural
  fork case, read a
    case zero
      send back
        read b
    case succ
      link ap
      send back
        make succ
          bind prior
            call plus
              read ap
              read b

task times
  take a, like natural
  take b, like natural
  like natural
  fork case, read a
    case zero
      send back
        make zero
    case succ
      link ap
      send back
        call plus
          read b
          call times
            read ap
            read b

# THE DIVISOR-SUM LAW: a number dividing two others divides their sum. If a = d j and b = d k, then a + b = d (j + k),
# which is the distributive law times d (plus j k) = plus (times d j) (times d k). Proved by induction on d. So the set of
# multiples of d is closed under addition (it is a subgroup), the fact behind ideals and modular arithmetic.
rule divisors-closed-under-sum
  mark d, like natural
  mark j, like natural
  mark k, like natural
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call times
        read d
        call plus
          read j
          read k
      call plus
        call times
          read d
          read j
        call times
          read d
          read k
  fold d

# TWO DIVIDES SIX: 6 = 2 times 3, the witness quotient is 3.
rule two-divides-six
  find q, like natural
    make succ
      bind prior
        make succ
          bind prior
            make succ
              bind prior
                make zero
  show hold
    call is-equal
      make succ
        bind prior
          make succ
            bind prior
              make succ
                bind prior
                  make succ
                    bind prior
                      make succ
                        bind prior
                          make succ
                            bind prior
                              make zero
      call times
        make succ
          bind prior
            make succ
              bind prior
                make zero
        read q
  calm

# THREE DIVIDES SIX: 6 = 3 times 2.
rule three-divides-six
  find q, like natural
    make succ
      bind prior
        make succ
          bind prior
            make zero
  show hold
    call is-equal
      make succ
        bind prior
          make succ
            bind prior
              make succ
                bind prior
                  make succ
                    bind prior
                      make succ
                        bind prior
                          make succ
                            bind prior
                              make zero
      call times
        make succ
          bind prior
            make succ
              bind prior
                make succ
                  bind prior
                    make zero
        read q
  calm

# TWO DIVIDES FOUR: 4 = 2 times 2.
rule two-divides-four
  find q, like natural
    make succ
      bind prior
        make succ
          bind prior
            make zero
  show hold
    call is-equal
      make succ
        bind prior
          make succ
            bind prior
              make succ
                bind prior
                  make succ
                    bind prior
                      make zero
      call times
        make succ
          bind prior
            make succ
              bind prior
                make zero
        read q
  calm

# EVERY NUMBER DIVIDES ZERO: 0 = d times 0, the witness quotient is zero. Zero is a multiple of everything.
rule everything-divides-zero
  mark d, like natural
  find q, like natural
    make zero
  show hold
    call is-equal
      make zero
      call times
        read d
        read q
  calm